RCLS R.00
RTN
@ ======== the move generator ========
@ ---- LBL :GEN: the moves of the colour R32. R39: 1 all of them and castling, 0 all of them, 2 the captures only,
@ 3 each move valued at once (LBL :QEVAL:, LBL :CEVAL:) until the cut R70 (the other modes set R70 = 0), the squares
@ from the colour's own side (black: 99 down to 22; R99 the step +1 / -1: the order of the replies does not change
@ the answer, and the pieces that can reply are reached first). Into
@ the row R38 of ML: the captures from
@ column 1 (R37 of them, by the value taken: LBL :ADD:), the others from column 120 down (R72 of them); LBL :MLK:
@ reads the k-th in that order.
@ The squares 22-99 in order, counted down by DSE 31 (up: 78 to 1, the square 100 - R31; down: 99.021, the square
@ IP R31; the cut sets R31 = 0: the loop ends); a piece of the colour: x = its piece x the colour is 1-6
@ (|x - 3.5| <= 2.5: the border 8 x the colour is +-8, out) ----
LBL 00                          ; :GEN:
0
STO 37
0
STO 72
RCL 39
3
X≠Y?
IF 11
  0
  STO 70
ENDIF 11
1
STO 99
RCL 39
3
X=Y?
IF 12
  RCL 32
  STO 99
ENDIF 12
RCL 99
X>0?
IF 13
  78
  STO 31
  DO 02
    100
    RCL- 31
    STO 30
    1
    RCL 30
    STOIJ
    RCLEL
    RCL× 32
    STO 34
    3.5
    -
    ABS
    2.5
    X≥Y?
    XEQ 01                      ; -> :GENSQ:
    DSE 31
  WHILE 02
  ENDDO 02
ELSE 13
  99.021
  STO 31
  DO 03
    RCL 31
    IP
    STO 30
    1
    RCL 30
    STOIJ
    RCLEL
    RCL× 32
    STO 34
    3.5
    -
    ABS
    2.5
    X≥Y?
    XEQ 01                      ; -> :GENSQ:
    DSE 31
  WHILE 03
  ENDDO 03
ENDIF 13
RTN
