@ ---- LBL :MAKE: plays R40 at the ply R46: the undo data in the row R46 of UN (the move, the piece, the piece
@ taken, the en passant square, SC, the flag) and R56 + R46 (the castling word); SC by the values of PT; en
@ passant (the pawn behind the target), promotion (a queen on the row 5.5 + 3.5 c), castling (the rook too),
@ the king's square, the new en passant square, the castling rights (LBL :CRSQ: on from and to), the side ----
